ld be the slope field for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x^{2} y^{2}?$"] [:db/add "fab6398f-c6bd-5a40-9707-cf9c4178811e" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we are given an equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is a function of $x$ and $y.$ This means that the slope varies with both $x$ and $y.$\n\nOf the given slope fields, the only one that varies with both $x$ and $y$ is the following:\n\n![](images/b3/b3238f0e3d45edb43f59c23b1001ee3718b7c72aa26825d93d717311ce2ae3f0.png)\n\n \n\nTo see this more clearly, notice that if we draw a vertical line and a horizontal line, the slopes vary if we move along either of the two lines.\n\n![](images/0e/0e5240b1aa25aac80cf8f73c4b4d3372ff2717579c460292662c861de648b6d3.png)"] [:db/add "fab6398f-c6bd-5a40-9707-cf9c4178811e" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [:db/add "fab6398f-c6bd-5a40-9707-cf9c4178811e" :question/answer-fields "8041184d-0204-5761-bb9c-f6e0c74be8d0"] [:db/ensure "fab6398f-c6bd-5a40-9707-cf9c4178811e" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186172040 :knowledge-point/questions "fab6398f-c6bd-5a40-9707-cf9c4178811e"] [:db/add "4d19a8e3-4c66-509c-bc85-ede8ff589c68" :answer/id #uuid "4d19a8e3-4c66-509c-bc85-ede8ff589c68"] [:db/add "4d19a8e3-4c66-509c-bc85-ede8ff589c68" :answer/type :answer.type/image] [:db/add "4d19a8e3-4c66-509c-bc85-ede8ff589c68" :answer/value "images/05/050e4af62def2e0bb11dd6da685802bc83f91c661db9d9620e0a68e07f0e4404.png"] [:db/ensure "4d19a8e3-4c66-509c-bc85-ede8ff589c68" :answer/validate] [:db/add "f59ed13f-9167-519e-b4ca-f80f95f341e0" :answer/id #uuid "f59ed13f-9167-519e-b4ca-f80f95f341e0"] [:db/add "f59ed13f-9167-519e-b4ca-f80f95f341e0" :answer/type :answer.type/image] [:db/add "f59ed13f-9167-519e-b4ca-f80f95f341e0" :answer/value "images/86/868591fceebe38d75b3bb202455f5c09256bf8516a4d9dd420f504e10ae7397c.png"] [:db/ensure "f59ed13f-9167-519e-b4ca-f80f95f341e0" :answer/validate] [:db/add "82402fa3-9